<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Králický Sněžník–Sušina circuit — Morava valley, Králický Sněžník, Sušina, Slaměnka and western walking return [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>From the last Upper Dolní Morava parking area, follow yellow markings up the Morava valley towards Sněžná chata, then the marked ascent past the former hut site and Morava spring to Králický Sněžník. Retrace the summit approach, follow red to Stříbrnická saddle, then blue over Stříbrnická, Sušina and Podbělka. Use the short green section and blue approach to the Slaměnka hut grounds, returning from that spur the same way. Complete the western walking return through Slon, Kolotoč, Kamila and Vista to the start, about 22.9 km in all. Carry a current map for the resort-road junctions, which are not all confirmed colour-marked. Use established marked paths and maintained boardwalks, protect fragile habitats and keep dogs leashed. Prefer dry, snow-free daylight; steep ground, wet wood, bog, fog and wind require care. Check current paths, huts and parking; postpone if any required leg is closed or unsafe, and do not use the northern route where walking is prohibited. No off-trail statue or tower trip, camping, fires, collecting or interior admission is included. Height-gain and walking-time figures are approximate; allow extra time for conditions and stops.

Route geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0 — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright; https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/. Complete source ways, nodes and walking parents supply 977 literal positions and 976 directed source edges. The five western Kamila–Vista edges retain the reference order of historical way 460017071 version 12 with explicitly selected latest-visible source node versions, including two deleted interior nodes’ last-visible versions and current shared endpoint 2899890707 version 6. This is an explicit mixed-version source-reference view, not an atomic historical snapshot or a claim that the deleted way is currently mapped; current responsible walking-route adoption independently supports the same walking ground. Source histories: https://api.openstreetmap.org/api/0.6/way/460017071/history. Only repeated identical shared junction positions are removed between directed slices. Canonical display uses the repository’s existing source-vertex simplifier; the complete default variant and private research GPX retain all literal source edges. No private guide, operator-track, government-polygon or raster coordinates, synthetic connectors, snaps, altered coordinates or elevations. Two-dimensional planning geometry; not navigation-grade or legal permission.

